  "review_summary": "Question 4 (Oscillations of a Liquid Column in a U-tube) verified with PASS across all 4 leaves (a), (b), (c)(i), and (c)(ii). Leaf (a) rigorously demonstrates simple harmonic motion by showing acceleration a = -(2g/L)x satisfies a proportional to -x since g and L are constants. Leaf (b) extracts oscillation period T = 0.50 s from Fig. 4.3 and equates omega^2 = (2*pi/T)^2 = 2g/L to determine liquid column length L = (2 * 9.81 * 0.50^2) / (4*pi^2) = 0.12 m. Leaf (c)(i) correctly identifies physical causes of damping including liquid viscosity, internal fluid friction, viscous drag, or tube wall friction. Leaf (c)(ii) evaluates total energy ratio after 1.5 cycles (t = 0.75 s) as (x_1.5 / x_0)^2 = (1.3 / 2.0)^2 = 0.42. Scaffolding, hints, teacher walkthrough, deterministic check tolerances, AI rubrics, curriculum taxonomy, and registry references are fully accurate and compliant.",
